                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: In order to keep something in their hand, a person needs to have a certain level of grip strength and control.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is grip strength?\n2. How can a person improve their grip strength?\n3. What are some techniques for holding onto something securely?\n\nAnswers:\n1. Grip strength is the amount of force a person can apply with their hand to hold onto an object.\n2. A person can improve their grip strength through exercises such as squeezing a stress ball or using hand grippers.\n3. Techniques for holding onto something securely include making a fist around the object, using all fingers to grip the object, and keeping the wrist straight and stable.\n\nAnswer to original question: To keep something in their hand, a person should use a combination of grip strength and control techniques such as making a fist or using all fingers to grip the object.",
