                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Step-by-step procedure:\n1. Identify the task: What does a kindergarten teacher do before nap time?\n2. Brainstorm possible actions a teacher might take before nap time.\n3. Evaluate each option based on what a teacher would typically do and what would be most beneficial for the students.\n4. Choose the best option based on the evaluation.\n\nGoing through each option:\nA) Lower expectations - This is not a helpful action for a teacher to take before nap time. It may lead to students feeling discouraged or unmotivated.\nB) Encourage - This is a helpful action for a teacher to take before nap time. Encouragement can help students feel positive and relaxed before nap time.\nC) Fear - This is not a helpful action for a teacher to take before nap time. Fear can lead to anxiety and stress, which is not conducive to a good nap.\nD) Time test - This is not a helpful action for a teacher to take before nap time. A time test may cause students to feel rushed or anxious, which is not conducive to a good nap.\nE) Tell story - This is a helpful action for a teacher to take before nap time. A story can help students feel calm and relaxed before nap time.\n\nBased on the evaluation, the best option is E) tell story.",
