                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Leafy greens are a good source of minerals such as iron, calcium, and magnesium. However, there are other sources of minerals that can be obtained through diet or supplements.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What minerals are important for the body?\n2. What are some non-leafy green sources of these minerals?\n3. What is a multivitamin and can it provide necessary minerals?\n4. Can minerals be obtained from farms or the earth?\n5. What is ore and can it be a source of minerals for humans?\n\nAnswers:\n1. Important minerals for the body include iron, calcium, magnesium, potassium, and zinc.\n2. Non-leafy green sources of these minerals include dairy products, nuts, seeds, beans, whole grains, seafood, and meat.\n3. A multivitamin is a dietary supplement that contains a combination of vitamins and minerals. It can provide necessary minerals, but it is important to choose a high-quality supplement and not rely solely on it for nutrient intake.\n4. Minerals can be obtained from farms through consuming animal products or crops that are rich in minerals. Minerals can also be obtained from the earth through consuming mineral-rich water or salt.\n5. Ore is a naturally occurring material that contains minerals. While some ores can be consumed by humans, it is not a recommended source of minerals as it may contain harmful substances and is not easily digestible.",
