                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "To answer this question, we need to carefully read and understand what is being asked. The question is asking about the type of taxes that Joe owed in addition to back taxes. \n\nFirst, we need to understand what back taxes are. Back taxes are taxes that were not paid in previous years and are now overdue. \n\nNext, we need to consider the answer choices and determine which one makes the most sense. \n\nA) Anterior - This word refers to something that is located towards the front of the body. It does not make sense in the context of taxes. \n\nB) Front - This word is similar to anterior and also does not make sense in the context of taxes. \n\nC) Main - This word could potentially make sense, as it could refer to the primary or most important type of taxes that Joe owed. However, without more information, we cannot be certain. \n\nD) Front - This is a repeat of answer choice B and can be eliminated. \n\nE) Current - This word refers to something that is happening now or in the present. It does not make sense in the context of back taxes, which are overdue. \n\nBased on this analysis, the most likely answer is C) main. However, without more information, we cannot be certain. It is possible that Joe owed multiple types of taxes in addition to back taxes.",
