                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Rephrased question: What is the most common location for people to make coffee?\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n\n1. Coffee shops are a popular place to buy coffee, but the question is asking where people make coffee, not buy it. Therefore, we can eliminate option A.\n\n2. Offices often have coffee machines or communal coffee areas, so this could be a possibility. However, not everyone works in an office, so it may not be the most common location. We'll keep option B as a possibility for now.\n\n3. Tables are not typically a place where people make coffee, so we can eliminate option C.\n\n4. Washing has nothing to do with making coffee, so we can eliminate option D.\n\n5. Kitchens are a common location for making coffee, as most households have a coffee maker or some other method of brewing coffee. This seems like the most likely answer, so we'll choose option E.\n\nAnswer: E) kitchen",
