                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Step-by-step procedure:\n1. Identify the question: Where do most people turn to get information on their phones?\n2. List the possible answers: A) internet, B) book, C) online, D) google, E) manual.\n3. Determine the most likely answer based on common knowledge and personal experience.\n4. Verify the answer by conducting research or finding reliable sources.\n\nGoing through each step:\n1. The question is clearly stated.\n2. The possible answers are listed.\n3. Based on common knowledge and personal experience, the most likely answer is A) internet or D) google.\n4. To verify the answer, we can conduct research by looking at statistics or surveys on where people turn to for information on their phones. According to a survey conducted by Pew Research Center in 2015, 64% of American adults own a smartphone and 62% of smartphone owners have used their phone in the past year to look up information about a health condition. Additionally, a survey conducted by Google in 2018 found that 96% of smartphone users have used their phone to get information on the go, with 3 in 4 users turning to search engines first. These statistics support the answer of A) internet or D) google as the most likely answer.",
