                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: In today's digital age, smartphones have become an essential part of our lives. People use their phones for various purposes, including communication, entertainment, and information gathering. \n\nSub-questions:\n1. What kind of information do people usually look for on their phones?\n2. What are the different sources of information available on phones?\n3. Which source of information is the most popular among phone users?\n\nAnswering sub-question 1: People usually look for a wide range of information on their phones, including news, weather updates, sports scores, social media updates, directions, and product reviews.\n\nAnswering sub-question 2: The different sources of information available on phones include the internet, apps, social media, and search engines.\n\nAnswering sub-question 3: Based on the given options, the most popular source of information on phones is the internet. This is because the internet provides access to a vast amount of information on any topic, and most smartphones come with built-in web browsers. While Google is a popular search engine, it is just one of the many ways people access the internet on their phones. Therefore, option A (internet) is the correct answer to the original question.",
