                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: A dictionary is a reference book that contains an alphabetical list of words with information about their meanings, pronunciations, and usage. It is commonly used to look up the meaning of words that are unfamiliar or unclear.\n\nAdditional facts: Borrowing books is a common practice in libraries, where patrons can check out books for a limited period of time and return them when they are done. Libraries often organize their collections by subject or genre, and may have separate sections for fiction, non-fiction, reference books, and other materials.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is a dictionary?\n2. What is borrowing?\n3. What are the common places where books can be borrowed?\n4. How are libraries organized?\n5. Where would a dictionary be located in a library?\n\nAnswers:\n1. A dictionary is a reference book that contains an alphabetical list of words with information about their meanings, pronunciations, and usage.\n2. Borrowing is the act of temporarily taking something with the intention of returning it later.\n3. Books can be borrowed from libraries, classrooms, friends, family, and bookstores.\n4. Libraries are often organized by subject or genre, with separate sections for fiction, non-fiction, reference books, and other materials.\n5. A dictionary would be located in the reference section of a library, along with other reference books such as encyclopedias, atlases, and almanacs. It may also be located in the language or linguistics section, depending on the library's organization.",
