                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Hair loss is a common concern for many men as they age. It is often caused by a combination of genetics and hormonal changes.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What causes hair loss in men?\n2. Is hair loss preventable?\n3. What are the different types of hair loss?\n4. How can hair loss be treated?\n\nAnswer:\n1. Hair loss in men is caused by a combination of genetics and hormonal changes. Specifically, the hormone dihydrotestosterone (DHT) can cause hair follicles to shrink, leading to thinner and shorter hair over time.\n2. While hair loss may not be completely preventable, there are steps that can be taken to slow down the process. These include maintaining a healthy diet, avoiding harsh hair treatments, and reducing stress.\n3. There are several types of hair loss, including male pattern baldness, alopecia areata, and telogen effluvium. Male pattern baldness is the most common type and is characterized by a receding hairline and thinning hair on the crown of the head.\n4. Hair loss can be treated with medications such as minoxidil and finasteride, which can help to slow down or even reverse the process. Hair transplant surgery is also an option for those who have experienced significant hair loss.",
                        "answers": [
