                        "cot": "Additional knowledge: Performing for the first time can refer to any type of performance, such as a musical performance, a speech, or a sports game.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is the definition of performing for the first time?\n2. What are some common emotions people experience when performing for the first time?\n3. What factors can influence the type of feeling someone experiences when performing for the first time?\n\nAnswers:\n1. Performing for the first time refers to the act of presenting or showcasing a skill or talent in front of an audience for the first time.\n2. Common emotions people experience when performing for the first time include anxiety, nervousness, excitement, fear, and anticipation.\n3. Factors that can influence the type of feeling someone experiences when performing for the first time include the individual's personality, past experiences with performing, the size and type of audience, the level of preparation, and the importance of the performance. \n\nAnswer: E) anxiety is the type of feeling that performing for the first time is likely to produce, although other emotions such as nervousness and excitement may also be present.",
