                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Can you explain what you mean by staying healthy?\n\nProfessor: Sure, staying healthy means taking care of your body and mind to prevent illnesses and maintain overall well-being.\n\nStudent: Okay, so what are some things a person can do to take care of their body and mind?\n\nProfessor: One important thing is to eat every day, which is option B. This means having a balanced diet with plenty of fruits, vegetables, whole grains, and lean proteins.\n\nStudent: What about option A, fever? Is that related to staying healthy?\n\nProfessor: No, actually having a fever is a symptom of an illness, not a way to stay healthy. It's important to monitor your body temperature and seek medical attention if you have a fever.\n\nStudent: And what about option C, excited? Can being excited help you stay healthy?\n\nProfessor: Well, being excited can certainly boost your mood and mental health, but it's not necessarily a direct way to stay physically healthy. It's important to find ways to manage stress and maintain a positive outlook, but that's just one aspect of overall health.\n\nStudent: I see. And what about options D and E, headache and expressive?\n\nProfessor: Similar to fever, having a headache is a symptom of an underlying issue and not a way to stay healthy. And while being expressive and creative can certainly contribute to overall well-being, it's not a direct way to maintain physical health. \n\nSo, in summary, the best way to stay healthy is to eat a balanced diet, exercise regularly, get enough sleep, manage stress, and seek medical attention when necessary.",
