                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "it is important to note that hamburger itself is not inherently deadly. However, there are several ways that consuming hamburger could potentially lead to death:\n\nC) Mad cow disease: If the hamburger is contaminated with prions, which are misfolded proteins that cause a fatal brain disease called Creutzfeldt-Jakob disease (CJD), also known as mad cow disease.\n\nA) Gas: If the hamburger is not cooked properly, it could contain harmful bacteria such as E. coli or Salmonella, which can cause severe food poisoning and potentially lead to death.\n\nD) Death: In rare cases, people with severe allergies to certain ingredients in the hamburger, such as peanuts or soy, could experience a life-threatening allergic reaction called anaphylaxis.\n\nOverall, it is important to handle and cook hamburger properly to avoid any potential health risks.",
                        "answers": [
