                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nOption A and B are not possible causes of death from eating a hamburger. Option E is also not a cause of death, as feeling full is a normal bodily response to eating. Option D is too vague and does not provide a specific cause of death.\n\nThe correct answer is C) mad cow disease. If the hamburger meat is contaminated with the prion that causes mad cow disease, also known as bovine spongiform encephalopathy (BSE), it can lead to a fatal brain disease called variant Creutzfeldt-Jakob disease (vCJD) in humans who consume it. However, it is important to note that cases of vCJD are extremely rare and strict regulations and testing procedures are in place to prevent contaminated meat from entering the food supply.",
