                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Step-by-step procedure:\n1. Identify the potential causes of death from eating hamburger.\n2. Evaluate each potential cause based on scientific evidence and likelihood.\n3. Determine the most probable cause of death.\n\nGoing through each step:\n1. The potential causes of death from eating hamburger are gas, getting full, mad cow disease, and death (which is not a specific cause but rather a general outcome).\n2. Gas is unlikely to cause death from eating hamburger. Getting full may cause discomfort or other health issues, but is not likely to result in death. Mad cow disease is a rare but serious illness that can be contracted from contaminated beef, but it is also unlikely to cause death. Therefore, death itself is the most probable cause of death from eating hamburger, although the specific cause of death may vary (e.g. choking, allergic reaction, food poisoning).\n3. Based on the evaluation of each potential cause, death is the most probable outcome of eating hamburger that results in fatality.",
