                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The correct answer is C) breathing.\n\nWhen someone is dead, their body ceases to function. This means that they stop breathing, their heart stops beating, and their brain activity ceases. Breathing is a vital function of the body, and without it, the body cannot survive. Therefore, when someone is dead, they stop breathing. \n\nOption A) moving is not necessarily true as some muscles can still contract after death due to rigor mortis. \nOption B) working is not specific enough as it could refer to any type of work, not just physical labor. \nOption D) alive is not something that someone stops doing when they are dead, as being alive is the opposite of being dead. \nOption E) deadworks is not a term or concept that exists.",
