                        "cot": "How do bodily functions change when a person dies?\nA) The body stops moving.\nB) The person no longer works.\nC) Breathing ceases.\nD) The person is no longer alive.\nE) There is no such thing as \"deadworks.\"\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n- When a person dies, their body stops functioning.\n- The heart stops beating, which means blood no longer circulates through the body.\n- Without blood flow, the body's cells stop receiving oxygen and nutrients, which causes them to die.\n- The brain also stops functioning, which means the person is no longer conscious or able to move.\n- Therefore, the correct answer is A) moving.\n\nAnswer: A) moving.",
