                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Can you explain what you mean by \"drinking alcohol leads to\"?\n\nProfessor: Sure, when someone consumes alcohol, it can have various effects on their body and behavior. Some of these effects can be positive, such as feeling more relaxed or having fun, but there can also be negative consequences.\n\nStudent: What are some of the negative consequences?\n\nProfessor: Well, some common negative effects of drinking alcohol include intoxication, vomiting, drinking more alcohol, and nausea.\n\nStudent: Can you explain what you mean by intoxication?\n\nProfessor: Intoxication is when someone has consumed enough alcohol to impair their judgment, coordination, and ability to think clearly. This can lead to risky behavior, accidents, and even alcohol poisoning in severe cases.\n\nStudent: And what about vomiting and nausea?\n\nProfessor: Vomiting and nausea are common side effects of drinking too much alcohol. When someone drinks too much, their body may try to expel the alcohol by vomiting. Nausea can also occur as a result of the body's reaction to the alcohol.\n\nStudent: So, drinking more alcohol is also a negative consequence?\n\nProfessor: Yes, drinking more alcohol can be a negative consequence of drinking alcohol. When someone drinks too much, they may lose control of their drinking and continue to consume more alcohol, which can lead to further negative consequences. It's important to drink responsibly and know your limits.",
