                        "cot": "\n\nC) Interrupted 2-0 polypropylene suture with supporting pledgets is the best definitive surgical approach to take in this patient.\n\nExplanation:\nThe patient has a full thickness penetrating injury to the right ventricular free wall, which is a life-threatening condition that requires immediate surgical intervention. Options A, B, D, and E are not appropriate in this situation. Immediate cardiac transplant (option A) is not feasible in this setting due to the lack of available organs and the patient's unstable condition. Watchful waiting while resuscitative fluids are initiated (option B) is not appropriate because the patient is bleeding profusely and requires immediate surgical intervention. Needle thoracostomy over the 2nd intercostal space (option D) is not appropriate because it is a temporary measure that only relieves tension pneumothorax and does not address the underlying cardiac injury. Surgical adhesive glue (option E) is not appropriate because it cannot repair a full thickness penetrating injury to the heart. Interrupted 2-0 polypropylene suture with supporting pledgets (option C) is the best definitive surgical approach to repair the cardiac injury and stop the bleeding.",
