                        "cot": "The question is asking for the class of immune cells that lyse abnormal cells without the need for opsonization, priming, or prior activation. To answer this question, we need to identify the immune cells that fit this description.\n\nStep 1: Identify the characteristics of the immune cells in question.\n- Lyse abnormal cells without the need for opsonization, priming, or prior activation.\n\nStep 2: Identify the immune cells that fit these characteristics.\n- CD8+ T lymphocytes require priming and activation.\n- Bone marrow-derived macrophages require opsonization.\n- CD4+ T lymphocytes require priming and activation.\n- Natural killer cells fit the description of lysing abnormal cells without the need for opsonization, priming, or prior activation.\n- Band neutrophils are not typically involved in lysing abnormal cells.\n\nStep 3: Select the best answer.\nThe answer is D) Natural killer cells.",
