                    {
                        "id": "5fe6d1d6-8478-42ed-9b9b-5bc2a4bbbe32",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-16",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Monoclonal gammopathy is a condition in which an abnormal protein called monoclonal protein is produced by plasma cells. Peripheral neuropathy is a common symptom of monoclonal gammopathy. Serum protein electrophoresis is a test used to detect monoclonal gammopathy. A bone marrow biopsy is used to determine the percentage of monoclonal plasma cells in the bone marrow. Downregulation of class I major histocompatibility molecules in monoclonal plasma cells can help them evade the immune system.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is the function of class I major histocompatibility molecules?\n2. What is the role of immune cells in preventing the proliferation of abnormal cells?\n3. What are the characteristics of CD8+ T lymphocytes, bone marrow-derived macrophages, CD4+ T lymphocytes, natural killer cells, and band neutrophils?\n\nAnswers:\n1. Class I major histocompatibility molecules are found on the surface of all nucleated cells and present peptides derived from intracellular proteins to CD8+ T lymphocytes. This allows the immune system to detect and eliminate cells that are infected with viruses or have become cancerous.\n2. Natural killer cells are a class of immune cells that can lyse abnormal cells without the need for opsonization, priming, or prior activation. They recognize cells that have downregulated class I major histocompatibility molecules, which is a common strategy used by cancer cells to evade the immune system.\n3. CD8+ T lymphocytes are a type of immune cell that recognize and eliminate cells that are infected with viruses or have become cancerous. Bone marrow-derived macrophages are a type of immune cell that engulf and digest foreign particles, such as bacteria and dead cells. CD4+ T lymphocytes are a type of immune cell that help coordinate the immune response by activating other immune cells. Band neutrophils are immature neutrophils that are released from the bone marrow in response to infection or inflammation.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "00adb4c0-2a02-43eb-a861-11a473982ac7",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-E",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "D) Natural killer cells, as they are the class of immune cells that can lyse abnormal cells without the need for opsonization, priming, or prior activation, and recognize cells that have downregulated class I major histocompatibility molecules.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "D",
                                "correct_answer": true
                            }
                        ],
                        "author": "thoughtsource",
                        "date": "2023/03/30 03:51:14",
                        "api_service": "openai_chat",
                        "model": "{'name': 'gpt-3.5-turbo', 'temperature': 0, 'max_tokens': 512}",
                        "comment": "",
