                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Identify the key information in the question.\n- A 67-year-old man with peripheral neuropathy has monoclonal gammopathy.\n- Bone marrow biopsy shows 6% monoclonal plasma cells.\n- Class I major histocompatibility molecules are downregulated in these monoclonal plasma cells.\n- The proliferation of these monoclonal plasma cells is normally prevented by a class of immune cells that lyse abnormal cells without the need for opsonization, priming, or prior activation.\n\nStep 2: Recall the function of different immune cells.\n- CD8+ T lymphocytes: cytotoxic T cells that recognize and kill infected or abnormal cells.\n- Bone marrow-derived macrophages: phagocytic cells that engulf and digest foreign substances and cellular debris.\n- CD4+ T lymphocytes: helper T cells that activate and coordinate other immune cells.\n- Natural killer cells: innate immune cells that recognize and kill infected or abnormal cells without prior activation.\n- Band neutrophils: immature neutrophils that are released from the bone marrow during infection or inflammation.\n\nStep 3: Determine which class of immune cells matches the description in the question.\n- The immune cells in question are able to lyse abnormal cells without the need for opsonization, priming, or prior activation. This suggests an innate immune response, rather than an adaptive immune response.\n- Among the options given, natural killer cells are the only innate immune cells that fit this description. They are able to recognize and kill abnormal cells, including tumor cells and virus-infected cells, without prior activation or specific recognition.\n\nStep 4: Check that the answer is supported by the information in the question.\n- The question states that the proliferation of monoclonal plasma cells is normally prevented by a class of immune cells that lyse abnormal cells without the need for opsonization, priming, or prior activation.\n- The answer choice D, natural killer cells, matches this description and is therefore the correct answer.\n\nAnswer: D) Natural killer cells.",
