                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Let's use step by step inductive reasoning, given the medical nature of the question. \n\nThe question stem tells us that the proliferation of monoclonal plasma cells is prevented by a class of immune cells. This class of immune cells does not require opsonization, priming, or prior activation in order to lyse abnormal cells. \n\nFrom this, we can infer that the class of immune cells in question are natural killer cells. Natural killer cells are a type of lymphocyte that are part of the innate immune system. The innate immune system is the body's first line of defense against infection and disease. Natural killer cells are able to lyse abnormal cells without the need for opsonization, priming, or prior activation. \n\nTherefore, the best answer is C) Natural killer cells.",
