                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "A) Intrafascicular infiltration on muscle biopsy - This is not the most likely to confirm the diagnosis as it is not a characteristic finding in any specific muscle disease.\nB) Inflammation of synovial spaces on ultrasound - This finding is not relevant to the patient's symptoms and would not confirm the diagnosis.\nC) Perifascicular and perivascular infiltration on muscle biopsy - This is a characteristic finding in dermatomyositis, but the patient's symptoms and laboratory results are not consistent with this diagnosis.\nD) Positive anti-acetylcholine receptor antibodies - This finding is associated with myasthenia gravis, but the patient's symptoms and laboratory results are not consistent with this diagnosis.\nE) Dystrophin gene mutation on genetic analysis - This is the most likely to confirm the diagnosis as the patient's family history and symptoms are consistent with Duchenne's muscular dystrophy, which is caused by a mutation in the dystrophin gene.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is E) Dystrophin gene mutation on genetic analysis.",
