 family history. Duchenne's muscular dystrophy is an X-linked recessive disorder that affects boys and is characterized by progressive muscle weakness and wasting. The patient's maternal uncle died from this disorder, and the patient's symptoms and laboratory studies are consistent with a diagnosis of muscular dystrophy. A dystrophin gene mutation can confirm the diagnosis.",
