                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": " The first thing we need to do is confirm that this patient has Cushing's syndrome. We can do this with a 24-hour urinary cortisol level, which is elevated, or with a dexamethasone suppression test. The next step is to determine the cause of Cushing's syndrome. The most common cause is a pituitary adenoma, so the best next step is an MRI of the pituitary gland.",
