                    {
                        "id": "818a53e1-0b98-4c68-a563-bc445a6f2ffb",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-01",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nThe patient presents with fatigue and weakness that has been progressively worsening over the past four months. She also has hypertension, obesity, and abdominal striae. Her laboratory workup shows hyperglycemia, hypokalemia, and elevated urinary cortisol levels. Her serum cortisol levels do not decrease after a 48-hour high dose dexamethasone suppression trial. These findings suggest a diagnosis of Cushing's syndrome, which is caused by excess cortisol production.\n\nThe next step in management would be to determine the cause of the excess cortisol production. The most common cause of Cushing's syndrome is a pituitary adenoma that produces excess adrenocorticotropic hormone (ACTH), which stimulates the adrenal glands to produce cortisol. Therefore, an MRI of the pituitary gland (option C) would be the best next step in management to evaluate for a pituitary adenoma.\n\nOption A (MRI of the adrenal glands) would be considered if the patient had a history of adrenal tumors or if the pituitary MRI was negative. Option B (MRI of the chest) would be considered if the patient had a history of lung tumors or if there were clinical or radiographic findings suggestive of a lung tumor. Option D (low dose dexamethasone suppression test) is not necessary since the high dose suppression test was already performed and showed no suppression of cortisol levels. Option E (inferior petrosal sinus sampling) is a more invasive test that is reserved for cases where the pituitary MRI is negative or equivocal.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "b336acc9-13ec-4640-bed4-affff036c4b9",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-E",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "C) MRI of the pituitary gland.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "C",
                                "correct_answer": false
                            }
                        ],
                        "author": "thoughtsource",
                        "date": "2023/03/14 15:02:19",
