                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The patient presents with symptoms of fatigue, weakness, menstrual irregularities, obesity, abdominal striae, and hypertension. Her laboratory workup shows elevated glucose, high 24-hour urinary cortisol, high serum cortisol, and low ACTH levels. These findings are suggestive of Cushing's syndrome.\n\nThe 48-hour high dose dexamethasone suppression test did not show a decrease in her serum cortisol levels, which indicates that the cause of her Cushing's syndrome is not due to a pituitary adenoma (Cushing's disease). This is because a pituitary adenoma would typically suppress cortisol production in response to high-dose dexamethasone.\n\nGiven the low ACTH levels, the cause of her Cushing's syndrome is likely due to an adrenal source or an ectopic ACTH-producing tumor. An MRI of the adrenal glands (option A) would be the best next step in management to evaluate for an adrenal tumor. If the MRI does not reveal an adrenal tumor, further imaging of the chest (option B) may be necessary to evaluate for an ectopic ACTH-producing tumor. \n\nAn MRI of the pituitary gland (option C) would not be helpful in this case, as the high-dose dexamethasone suppression test has already ruled out a pituitary source. A low-dose dexamethasone suppression test (option D) would not provide any additional information, as the high-dose test has already been performed. Inferior petrosal sinus sampling (option E) is typically used to differentiate between pituitary and ectopic sources of ACTH when the cause of Cushing's syndrome is unclear, but in this case, the low ACTH levels and negative high-dose dexamethasone suppression test make a pituitary source unlikely.\n\nTherefore, the best next step in management is option A, an MRI of the adrenal glands.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "86c01d45-d654-41a8-8439-017dc29c0d63",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-E",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "A) MRI of the adrenal glands.",
