                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: A transvaginal ultrasound is a type of imaging test that uses high-frequency sound waves to create images of the inside of the body. It is commonly used to examine the female reproductive system, including the uterus and ovaries. An intrauterine mass refers to a mass located within the uterus.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is an intrauterine heteroechoic mass?\n2. What are anechoic spaces?\n3. What are the possible causes of an intrauterine mass with anechoic spaces and no identifiable fetus or amniotic fluid?\n4. What are the characteristics of chocolate cysts?\n5. What are the characteristics of corpus luteum cysts?\n6. What is a yolk sac tumor?\n7. What is a luteoma of pregnancy?\n8. What are the characteristics of theca lutein cysts?\n9. What are the characteristics of ovarian cysts with clear content?\n\nAnswers:\n1. An intrauterine heteroechoic mass refers to a mass located within the uterus that appears different from the surrounding tissue on ultrasound imaging.\n2. Anechoic spaces refer to areas within a mass or cyst that appear black on ultrasound imaging, indicating the absence of solid tissue or fluid.\n3. The possible causes of an intrauterine mass with anechoic spaces and no identifiable fetus or amniotic fluid include a molar pregnancy, a gestational trophoblastic tumor, or a hydropic fetus.\n4. Chocolate cysts, also known as endometriomas, are cysts that form when endometrial tissue grows outside of the uterus and attaches to the ovary. They are filled with old blood that has a dark, chocolate-like appearance.\n5. Corpus luteum cysts are cysts that form on the ovary after an egg has been released during ovulation. They are filled with fluid and can cause pain or discomfort.\n6. A yolk sac tumor is a rare type of ovarian cancer that typically occurs in young women. It is named for its resemblance to the yolk sac of an embryo.\n7. A luteoma of pregnancy is a benign tumor that can develop on the ovary during pregnancy. It is caused by an overgrowth of cells that produce hormones.\n8. Theca lutein cysts are cysts that form on the ovary in response to high levels of hormones, such as those seen in women with certain types of infertility or in women who are taking fertility drugs. They",
