                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nC) Deficiency in protein C\n\nThe patient's history of a previous thrombus and the presence of an inherited condition suggest a genetic predisposition to thrombosis. Protein C deficiency is a known genetic risk factor for thrombosis. Protein C is a natural anticoagulant that inhibits clotting factors and prevents excessive clot formation. Deficiency in protein C leads to a prothrombotic state, increasing the risk of thrombosis. The patient's symptoms and ultrasound findings are consistent with deep vein thrombosis (DVT), which is a common manifestation of thrombosis. Elevated serum homocysteine, thrombin inhibitor deficiency, auto-antibodies directed against phospholipids, and resistance to clotting factor degradation are all potential causes of thrombosis, but they are less likely in this patient given her clinical presentation and history.",
