                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Can you explain what a thrombus is?\n\nProfessor: A thrombus is a blood clot that forms in a blood vessel.\n\nStudent: What is the popliteal vein?\n\nProfessor: The popliteal vein is a vein located behind the knee.\n\nStudent: What is a genetic workup?\n\nProfessor: A genetic workup is a series of tests that are done to determine if a person has any genetic abnormalities or mutations.\n\nStudent: What is the inherited condition that the patient has?\n\nProfessor: The question does not provide us with that information, so we cannot answer that question.\n\nStudent: What is the role of protein C in the body?\n\nProfessor: Protein C is a natural anticoagulant that helps to prevent blood clots from forming.\n\nStudent: How does a deficiency in protein C lead to blood clots?\n\nProfessor: A deficiency in protein C can lead to blood clots because there is not enough of the anticoagulant present to prevent the formation of clots.\n\nStudent: What is the most likely pathophysiology of this patient\u2019s condition?\n\nProfessor: The most likely pathophysiology of this patient\u2019s condition is C) Deficiency in protein C, as a deficiency in this anticoagulant can lead to the formation of blood clots.",
                        "answers": [
