                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nC) The mischarged tRNA with valine will be incorporated in the codons that specify for lysine.\n\nExplanation: The ribosome does not have proofreading mechanisms to check whether the amino acid charged on the tRNA is correct or not. It only checks whether the anticodon on the tRNA matches the codon on the mRNA. In this case, since the mRNA contains only codons for lysine, the ribosome will use the mischarged Lys-tRNA with valine to incorporate valine instead of lysine into the growing peptide chain. This will result in a protein with a valine residue instead of lysine at the corresponding position.",
