                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Rephrased question: What medication was most likely recommended by the pain management team to reduce the opioid need of a 65-year-old man with metastatic lung cancer who is experiencing severe, unremitting pain and is having dose limiting side-effects from oral morphine?\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n- The patient has metastatic lung cancer and is experiencing severe, unremitting pain.\n- He has required escalating doses of oral morphine, but is now having dose limiting side-effects.\n- The pain management team recommends using a medication that can reduce his opioid need through interaction with the NMDA-receptor.\n- The most likely recommended agent would be one that interacts with the NMDA-receptor.\n- Among the options given, only Ketamine is known to interact with the NMDA-receptor.\n- Therefore, the most likely recommended agent is Ketamine.\n\nAnswer: B) Ketamine",
