                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Can you explain what metastatic lung cancer is?\n\nProfessor: Metastatic lung cancer is a type of cancer that starts in the lungs and then spreads to other parts of the body.\n\nStudent: What are dose limiting side-effects?\n\nProfessor: Dose limiting side-effects are side-effects that prevent the patient from being able to tolerate higher doses of a medication. In this case, the patient is experiencing side-effects from the oral morphine that are preventing him from being able to take higher doses to manage his pain.\n\nStudent: What is the NMDA-receptor?\n\nProfessor: The NMDA-receptor is a type of receptor in the brain that is involved in the perception of pain. By interacting with this receptor, certain medications can help to reduce the amount of opioids needed to manage pain.\n\nStudent: What is propofol?\n\nProfessor: Propofol is a medication that is commonly used for sedation during medical procedures. It is not typically used for pain management.\n\nStudent: What is fentanyl?\n\nProfessor: Fentanyl is a powerful opioid medication that is often used for pain management. However, in this case, the patient is experiencing dose limiting side-effects from oral morphine, so the pain management team is looking for an alternative medication.\n\nStudent: What is ketorolac?\n\nProfessor: Ketorolac is a nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drug (NSAID) that is used for pain management. However, it does not interact with the NMDA-receptor, so it is not the most likely recommended agent in this case.\n\nStudent: What is midazolam?\n\nProfessor: Midazolam is a medication that is commonly used for sedation and anxiety relief. It is not typically used for pain management.\n\nStudent: So, the most likely recommended agent is ketamine?\n\nProfessor: Yes, that's correct. Ketamine is a medication that can interact with the NMDA-receptor and help to reduce the amount of opioids needed to manage pain. It is often used in cases where patients are experiencing dose limiting side-effects from other pain medications.",
