                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Identify the condition described in the question.\nThe stillborn infant has a small pelvis, shallow intergluteal cleft, club feet, and absence of the sacrum and lumbar vertebrae. This constellation of findings is consistent with a diagnosis of caudal regression syndrome.\n\nStep 2: Identify the strongest predisposing factor for caudal regression syndrome.\nCaudal regression syndrome is a rare congenital disorder that affects the development of the lower half of the body. The strongest predisposing factor for this condition is maternal diabetes. Maternal diabetes can cause vascular damage to the developing fetus, leading to decreased blood flow and oxygenation to the lower half of the body. This can result in the malformation of the sacrum, lumbar vertebrae, and lower extremities, as seen in caudal regression syndrome.\n\nStep 3: Evaluate the answer choices.\nA) Maternal oligohydramnios: Oligohydramnios (low amniotic fluid) can be a contributing factor to caudal regression syndrome, but it is not the strongest predisposing factor.\nB) Intrauterine alcohol exposure: Alcohol exposure in utero can cause a range of developmental abnormalities, but it is not typically associated with caudal regression syndrome.\nC) Chromosome 13 trisomy: Trisomy 13 (Patau syndrome) is a chromosomal disorder that can cause a range of developmental abnormalities, but it is not typically associated with caudal regression syndrome.\nD) Maternal diabetes: As discussed above, maternal diabetes is the strongest predisposing factor for caudal regression syndrome.\nE) Chromosome 18 trisomy: Trisomy 18 (Edwards syndrome) is a chromosomal disorder that can cause a range of developmental abnormalities, but it is not typically associated with caudal regression syndrome.\n\nStep 4: Select the correct answer.\nBased on the above analysis, the correct answer is D) Maternal diabetes.",
                        "answers": [
