                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-E",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "B) Primary respiratory acidosis. This is because the patient has a chronic respiratory condition (likely COPD) that is exacerbated by an acute illness, leading to difficulty breathing and a productive cough. The physical examination and chest X-ray findings support the diagnosis of COPD, which is characterized by impaired gas exchange and retention of carbon dioxide. The ABG in this patient is likely to show a low pH (acidosis) and high carbon dioxide levels (respiratory acidosis) due to impaired gas exchange and retention of carbon dioxide.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "B",
