                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Can you explain what FEV1/FVC ratio means?\n\nProfessor: Sure, FEV1 stands for forced expiratory volume in one second, which is the amount of air a person can forcefully exhale in one second. FVC stands for forced vital capacity, which is the total amount of air a person can exhale forcefully after taking a deep breath. The FEV1/FVC ratio is the percentage of the FVC that is exhaled in the first second of the forced exhalation. In healthy individuals, this ratio is usually around 80%.\n\nStudent: What does a ratio of 60% indicate?\n\nProfessor: A ratio of 60% indicates that the patient has a decreased ability to exhale air forcefully in the first second, which suggests an obstructive lung disease such as chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD).\n\nStudent: Can you explain what arterial blood gases are?\n\nProfessor: Arterial blood gases (ABG) are a test that measures the levels of oxygen, carbon dioxide, and other gases in the blood. It also measures the acidity (pH) of the blood. ABG is used to evaluate how well the lungs are functioning and to diagnose respiratory and metabolic disorders.\n\nStudent: So, what would be the most likely result of ABG in this patient?\n\nProfessor: Based on the patient's symptoms and physical examination findings, the most likely result of ABG would be primary respiratory acidosis. This is because the patient has a chronic obstructive lung disease, which impairs the ability to exhale carbon dioxide. The fever and productive cough suggest an acute exacerbation of the underlying lung disease, which further impairs the ability to exhale carbon dioxide. This leads to an accumulation of carbon dioxide in the blood, causing respiratory acidosis.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "fcf1767c-0327-4422-9a8b-fddd16fb2bcc",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-E",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "B) Primary respiratory acidosis.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "B",
                                "correct_answer": true
                            }
                        ],
