                        "cot_trigger": "lievin-01",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Let's derive the differential diagnosis step by step. \n\nThe patient has a productive cough, so we can rule out primary respiratory alkalosis. \n\nThe patient has a barrel-shaped chest and diminished breath sounds, so we can rule out primary respiratory acidosis. \n\nThe patient has a 60% FEV1/FVC ratio, so we can rule out compensatory respiratory acidosis. \n\nThe patient has a cold, so we can rule out anion gap metabolic acidosis with respiratory alkalosis. \n\nThis leaves us with compensatory respiratory alkalosis.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
