                        "cot": "\n\nE) Order an ACTH stimulation test\n\nThe patient's symptoms and physical exam findings suggest a possible adrenal insufficiency, which can be confirmed by an ACTH stimulation test. This test measures the adrenal gland's ability to produce cortisol in response to ACTH stimulation. If the test confirms adrenal insufficiency, then treatment with hydrocortisone and fludrocortisone can be initiated. Androgen replacement treatment is not indicated in this case.",
