                        "cot": "\n\nD) Polymerase chain reaction (PCR) would be used to detect the genetic material of HIV if the child had been infected. PCR is a highly sensitive technique that can detect even small amounts of viral genetic material in a sample. ELISA, Western blot, and rapid HIV antibody tests are used to detect antibodies produced by the body in response to HIV infection, but these tests may not be reliable in infants born to HIV-positive mothers due to the presence of maternal antibodies. Southern blot is a technique used to detect specific DNA sequences, but it is not commonly used for HIV diagnosis.",
