                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nDifficult. \n\nThe patient's symptoms suggest a possible diagnosis of systemic sclerosis (scleroderma), which is an autoimmune disease. To answer the question, we need to know which antibodies are commonly associated with systemic sclerosis. The correct answer is E) Anti-ribonucleoprotein, which is found in about 30-40% of patients with systemic sclerosis. Anti-cardiolipin antibodies are associated with antiphospholipid syndrome, which can cause recurrent miscarriages, but this is not the most likely diagnosis based on the patient's symptoms. Anti-centromere antibodies are associated with limited cutaneous systemic sclerosis, while anti-helicase and anti-histone antibodies are associated with other autoimmune diseases such as lupus.",
