ociated with gastrointestinal symptoms. Option E) Menetrier disease is a rare disorder that affects the stomach lining, causing excess mucus production and enlarged folds in the stomach wall. While it may cause abdominal pain and constipation, it is not typically associated with polyps or colonic mucosal outpouchings.\n\nTherefore, the most likely diagnosis based on the information provided is familial adenomatous polyposis (FAP), which is not listed as an answer choice. The closest answer choice is option C) Ehlers-Dan",
