ion may not be the best choice for her. \n\nD) Mirtazapine is a noradrenergic and specific serotonergic antidepressant (NaSSA) commonly used to treat depression and anxiety. It can cause side effects such as drowsiness, weight gain, and dry mouth. It may also increase the risk of suicidal thoughts and behaviors in some patients. However, mirtazapine may be a good option for this patient given her difficulty sleeping and lack of suicidal ideation. \n\nE) Citalop",
