 medication is a selective serotonin reuptake inhibitor (SSRI) and is commonly used to treat depression and anxiety. It is not known to worsen eating disorder symptoms. Therefore, it may be a reasonable option for this patient.\n\nTherefore, the medication that should be avoided in this patient is A) Duloxetine.",
